{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779982444,"nonce":"XwQlU+MhE/ZUWAgA1TQDEKhP2QM=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABECMgzw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/186#issuecomment-4565704911"},"message":"## On-boat test + verify plan — marine_nav stack landed 2026-05-28\n\nFive PRs on `unh_marine_navigation` `jazzy` since the last deployment. Test in roughly the order below; each section is self-contained but several share evidence (`ros2 bag record -a`, BT log, `/follow_path/_action/status`).\n\n### Evidence to capture (record before each test)\n\n```bash\nros2 bag record -a --include-hidden-topics -o deployment_2026-MM-DD\n```\n\nPlus the launch's `~/.ros/log/\u003claunch_id\u003e/*task_navigator*.log` (BT log) and `mavros/state` for GUIDED watchdog evidence.\n\n---\n\n### 1. PR #41 (#23) — TF extrapolation on multi-line goals — **clean line transitions**\n\n**Pre-fix field event**: `unh_echoboats_project11/docs/logs/2026/2026-04-27_dev_logs.md:421` — \"weird turn onto 3rd line\" on a multi-line survey; goal aborted at line transition because Nav2 `lookupTransform(..., path.header.stamp)` fell outside the TF buffer.\n\n**Test**: run a ≥3-line survey. Plan lines with ≥30 s of expected execution time between transitions (so the stale-stamp drift is meaningful by the time line 3 starts).\n\n**Verify**:\n- No `[follow_path]` `STATUS_ABORTED` at line transitions on `/\u003cns\u003e/follow_path/_action/status` other than ones we expect (e.g. recovery-exhausted; those route via #37, not stale-stamp).\n- BT log has no `transform_extrapolation_exception` / `extrapolation into the past` lines around line transitions.\n- Visual: no \"weird turn\" — the boat follows each line's path without veering during the handoff.\n\n**Regression watch**: clear → resend (the old workaround for #35) still works (it always did; making sure we didn't accidentally regress it). Goto override still cancels and re-routes cleanly.\n\n---\n\n### 2. PR #37 (#25) — `Switch` dispatch + `RecoveryNode` + `SetTaskFailed` — **no more silent done-on-fail**\n\n**Pre-fix symptom**: a matched but failing trackline (e.g. `FollowPath` ABORT from `SimpleProgressChecker` not seeing 0.5 m in 10 s — wind, current, low motor power) fell through the catchall `SetTaskDone \"SkipUnknownTaskType\"` → trackline recorded clean done, mission silently moved on.\n\n**Test**: force a `FollowPath` ABORT.\n- Easiest path: send a survey line with a goal pose in shallow / boundary-rich water where the boat will struggle to make 0.5 m progress in 10 s. Or set a survey speed lower than the local current.\n- Alternative: send a short survey line and stand on the throttle remote-disable (no thrust → SimpleProgressChecker trips).\n\n**Verify**:\n- BT log shows `RecoveryNode` invoked (look for `SurveyLineFollowRecovery`); `Wait` BT action runs (~5 s dwell); up to 3 retries.\n- After 3 exhausted retries the line is recorded `failed` (camp heartbeat shows `status: failed` on that task) — NOT silently marked done.\n- The MISSION continues: subsequent lines run normally even after a failed one. (Don't accept whole-mission abort as the expected behavior — only the one line fails.)\n- Survey-area / line-set: a sub-line failure within the loop doesn't abort the outer area.\n\n**Regression watch**: `GotoPose` (operator hard-stop \"go to here\") still cancels `FollowPath` as before — `CancelAllNavigation` is unchanged for `GotoPose`. Hover, Goto, normal `survey_line` dispatch still routes correctly.\n\n---\n\n### 3. PR #36 (#35) — reactive `SetPathFromTask` — **mid-line modify-and-resend works**\n\n**Pre-fix symptom**: operator modifies the current trackline (different endpoint, different speed) and re-sends the mission; heartbeat updates to the new task but boat keeps following the OLD line because the BT latched `{survey_path}` once at sequence entry. Pre-fix workaround was \"clear + re-send\" (clearing flips the type, forcing re-entry).\n\n**Test**:\n1. Start a survey line.\n2. While boat is mid-line (≥30 % through), modify line 1's endpoint or speed in camp and **re-send the mission** (no clear).\n3. Repeat for a few different modification flavors: endpoint moved, speed changed, both.\n\n**Verify**:\n- `/\u003cns\u003e/follow_path/_action/status` shows a goal-UUID transition (preempt cycle: `CANCELING → CANCELED → new EXECUTING`) within ~1 BT tick of the re-send.\n- No `STATUS_ABORTED` on `/\u003cns\u003e/follow_path/_action/status` from this preempt.\n- Boat picks up the modified line without backtracking to the original endpoint.\n- Heartbeat reflects the new task content immediately.\n\n**⚠️ Known limitation — #43 deferred**: this PR's reactive refresh also routes a **different task** (different task_id, different trackline, or any other task type) to its **nearest path point** without transiting to its start. For the deployment workflow that means:\n- **DO**: modify the current trackline and re-send (the case this PR fixes).\n- **AVOID until #43 lands**: mid-line re-send with a *different* task. If you need to switch tasks, let the current line complete first OR use Clear → re-send a different task. A re-sent far / opposite-direction line will produce a sharp turn or wrong-direction traversal.\n- See PR #36's \"Known limitation\" callout and issue #43 / PR #44 for the proper fix that's deferred until after this deployment.\n\n---\n\n### 4. PR #40 (#28) — line-transition zero-cmd window bounded — **no more FCU GUIDED-watchdog trips**\n\n**Pre-fix field event**: `unh_echoboats_project11#169` 2026-05-22 — line2→line3 transition produced a ~4 s uncommanded zero-`cmd_vel` window from the back-to-back `CancelFollowPath` → planner re-plan → next `FollowPath` accept. FCU's 3 s GUIDED watchdog tripped → reverted to MANUAL.\n\n**Test**: multi-line survey with several line-to-line transitions. Watch every transition.\n\n**Verify**:\n- `/\u003cns\u003e/cmd_vel_nav` (or `/\u003cns\u003e/piloting_mode/autonomous/cmd_vel`) has zero-cmd windows of **\u003c3 s** at line handoffs — target is \u003c 0.5 s after this fix.\n- `/\u003cns\u003e/mavros/state` stays `GUIDED` throughout (no GUIDED → MANUAL → GUIDED bounce).\n- BT log: `ExitHoverForNav` invoked at `NavigateThroughWaypoints` entry + `SurveyLine` entry (instead of `CancelAllNavigation` — the leading `CancelFollowPath` is what created the gap).\n- Worst-case plan retry: `ComputePathThroughPoses` exhausts at 4 attempts (was 20) and fails loudly to `SetTaskFailed` via #37's path, instead of silently stalling at 20 retries.\n\n**Operational measurement**: the sim bag from PR #36 verification (`.scratchpad/issue-35-sim/midline_switch_0.mcap` on dev workstation) showed pre-#28 windows of 0.5-1.0 s in sim. The field 4 s case is the worst-case extension. After this PR, expect field windows to be measurably closer to sim — capture cmd_vel at 50+ Hz and `numpy.diff(timestamp)` to find any \u003e 1 s gap.\n\n**Regression watch**: `GotoPose` still uses `CancelAllNavigation` (full cancel + hover-drop, operator-intended hard stop). Don't expect `GotoPose` to preempt smoothly — that's by design.\n\n---\n\n### 5. PR #45 (#42) — hover publisher race fix — **`ros2 bag` captures `hover_visualization`**\n\n**Pre-fix symptom**: `ros2 bag record` on any topic list including `/\u003cns\u003e/hover_visualization` printed a flood of `more than one type associated` ERROR lines and silently dropped the topic from the bag. Caused by DDS discovery seeing two `MarkerArray` type registrations during the brief publisher-recreation window inside `Hover::onRun`.\n\n**Test**:\n1. `ros2 bag record /\u003cns\u003e/hover_visualization` (or `-a` with the deployment recording config that already lists this topic — `bizzyboat.yaml:329`).\n2. Trigger `HoverTask` at least 3 times: send Hover override → wait for hover stabilization → send Goto / next survey → send Hover override again. Repeat the cycle.\n\n**Verify**:\n- No `[ERROR] [ROSBAG2_TRANSPORT]: Topic '/\u003cns\u003e/hover_visualization' has more than one type associated` lines in the recorder console output.\n- `ros2 bag info \u003cbagdir\u003e` shows a non-zero message count on `/\u003cns\u003e/hover_visualization`.\n- RViz still renders the hover marker live (no regression on the live-display path).\n\n**Operational impact**: bag forensics for hover-state behavior now works. Future incident investigations referencing `hover_visualization` (e.g. the `docs/analysis/2026-05-01/outage_events.md` outage references) will have the data.\n\n---\n\n### Deferred — not in this deployment\n\n- **#43** (PR #44 `[PLAN]`) — different-task mid-mission re-send must transit to its start. The avoid-this case in §3 above. Will land in a follow-up PR after this deployment.\n- **Sim continuity repros** for #40 (`\u003c3 s` zero-cmd window assertion) and #42 (multi-cycle hover-bag-record). Can be run before the next deployment if there's time on the dev workstation — both share the same `simulator_launch.py` setup that was used for the PR #36 verification.\n\n### Quick smoke-test order (if time is short)\n\n1. **Single survey line**: confirms nothing's catastrophically broken at the dispatch level.\n2. **Multi-line survey (≥3 lines)**: covers PR #41 (TF extrapolation) + PR #40 (line transitions) at once.\n3. **Mid-line modify-and-resend**: covers PR #36.\n4. **Hover-cycle bag check**: covers PR #45.\n5. **Forced FollowPath ABORT** (push the boat into a stuck condition): covers PR #37. Save for last — destructive to the run.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779982460,"nonce":"yS2kR3x03dKCvFp9z4qHcetEHxU=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABECMp4Q","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/186#issuecomment-4565707233"},"message":"## Additional must-verify: #19 multi-source SeaSurfaceLayer + global relay (PRs #20 / #35 / #193, all merged 2026-05-28)\n\nThree coordinated merges land for this deployment:\n- [rolker/unh_marine_perception#20](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/pull/20) — multi-source `SeaSurfaceLayer` (shared persistent log-odds buffer, all 4 cameras feed one cell), new `SeaSurfaceRelayLayer`, `published_topic`, validating live-tunable param callback (incl. new `min_grazing_angle_deg` cutoff).\n- [rolker/seafloor_echoboat_project11#35](https://github.com/rolker/seafloor_echoboat_project11/pull/35) — `sea_surface_relay` added to `global_costmap.plugins` in the base config so Smac sees sea-surface lethal cells.\n- [#193](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/193) — bizzy overlay: 4 `SeaSurfaceLayer` instances → 1 multi-source + `published_topic`.\n\nThe old per-camera layer instances are gone — there is now exactly one `sea_surface_layer` plugin in `local_costmap.plugins`. A wrong-state load (e.g., `make build` skipped on the deployment host, or only one of the three PRs reached gabby) will surface as one of the failure modes below.\n\n### Pre-launch checks (on gabby, before going to water)\n\n- [ ] **Build is current**: `git log -1` in `layers/main/sensors_ws/src/unh_marine_perception` shows `fd0f057` (Merge #20) or later. Same for `seafloor_echoboat_project11` and `unh_echoboats_project11/bizzyboat_project11`. Then `make build` clean.\n- [ ] **nav2 launches without pluginlib errors** with `model:=240` + the instance overlay (the smoke test in #20 covers the producer + relay `onInitialize` paths, but only against a default-sized costmap — real-world nav2 init is the load-bearing case).\n- [ ] **Local costmap loads one sea-surface plugin, not four**: `ros2 param list /bizzy/local_costmap/local_costmap | grep sea_surface` should show parameters only under `sea_surface_layer.*` (no `sea_surface_layer_forward.*`, `_port.*`, etc.).\n- [ ] **All 4 cameras are wired**: `ros2 param list /bizzy/local_costmap/local_costmap | grep sea_surface_layer.observation_sources` shows `[forward, port, starboard, aft]`. The 4 `\u003csource\u003e.segmentation_topic` / `.camera_info_topic` params resolve to the OAK topics. `ros2 node info /bizzy/local_costmap/local_costmap` shows 4 segmentation + 4 camera_info subscriptions.\n- [ ] **Producer is publishing**: `ros2 topic hz /bizzy/sea_surface/lethal_grid` shows ~5–20 Hz (the local-costmap update rate). The `published_topic` param wires it to the relay; an empty value would silently disable the publisher.\n- [ ] **Relay is subscribing**: `ros2 node info /bizzy/global_costmap/global_costmap` shows a subscription to `/bizzy/sea_surface/lethal_grid` from the `sea_surface_relay` plugin.\n\n### On-water acceptance\n\nThe signature regression #19 fixes was the small-buoy resume on the 2026-05-26 bag (episode #21): an obstacle marked by one camera disappeared as the boat turned and the buoy moved into a different camera's FOV, because each layer had a per-frame-wiped private buffer. After #19 the four cameras feed one shared buffer in `map_tide` with log-odds + decay.\n\n- [ ] **Persistence across FOV handoff**: drive past a single buoy at slow speed (~1 m/s) so it sweeps through multiple cameras' FOV. The lethal cell should NOT flicker; it should persist for at least a few seconds after the buoy leaves all FOVs and then decay smoothly.\n- [ ] **Cross-camera fusion**: position the boat so a buoy is in the FOV overlap region of two adjacent cameras (forward+port or forward+starboard). The lethal cell should cross the threshold faster than a single-camera observation of the same buoy at the same range — same cell, double the evidence rate.\n- [ ] **Global plan routes around buoys**: confirm RViz shows the Smac global plan now goes around buoys (it didn't pre-#19 — global only saw chart + inflation). If local sees an obstacle and global doesn't route around it, the relay isn't propagating.\n- [ ] **No shadow smear**: tall obstacles (other boats, channel markers) should mark a small cell at the waterline, not a long radial streak out to `maximum_range`. The waterline-contact-only projection (phase 3, restored in #20) is what fixed this.\n\n### On-water tuning (live, no rebuild)\n\nAll six are validated via `ros2 param set` on `/bizzy/local_costmap/local_costmap sea_surface_layer.\u003cparam\u003e \u003cvalue\u003e`. Invalid values are rejected with a clear `reason` — the safety layer's interpretation cannot be silently poisoned.\n\n| Param | Default | Tighten if… |\n|---|---|---|\n| `min_grazing_angle_deg` | `0.0` (off) | Long-range cells flicker as the boat pitches. At camera height 1.5 m: `2°→43 m`, `5°→17 m`, `10°→8.5 m` horizontal reach. Start at `2.0`, raise if noise persists. |\n| `lethal_threshold` | `1.0` | False positives (single-frame flashes mark lethal). Raise toward `clamp`. |\n| `lethal_threshold` | `1.0` | False negatives (real buoys never cross). Lower (but stay above `hit_log_odds = 0.85` or one hit becomes lethal). |\n| `decay_half_life_s` | `30.0` | Stale obstacles persist too long after they leave the FOV. Lower (e.g. `15.0`). Raise if obstacles disappear too fast during pauses. |\n| `maximum_range` | `150.0` | Buffer warns about reach mismatch with parent costmap size, or noise dominates beyond X m. |\n| `hit_log_odds` / `miss_log_odds` / `clamp` | tuning knobs for advanced cases | Last resort — affect every cell in the buffer. |\n\n### Hotfix path if it breaks at the boat\n\nField agents on gabby (no GitHub credentials, push to gitcloud only — see [`project_field_hosts_no_github_creds.md`](https://github.com/rolker/ros2_agent_workspace) in agent memory) can:\n\n1. **Disable the new layer entirely** (fall back to chart + inflation only — boat will plan blind against buoys, but nav2 itself stays up): edit `bizzyboat_project11/config/nav2_overlay.yaml`, set `sea_surface_layer.enabled: false` (or remove the layer from `local_costmap.plugins`). Same in `seafloor_echoboat_project11/echoboat_project11/config/nav2_params.base.yaml` for `sea_surface_relay`. Restart nav2.\n2. **Disable just the global relay** (Smac plans blind, but local Collision Monitor still sees obstacles): same edit but only `sea_surface_relay.enabled: false`.\n3. **Revert the bizzy overlay only** (back to the 4-instance pre-#19 config): `git revert \u003cmerge_sha\u003e` of [#193](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/193) in `unh_echoboats_project11`. Note this still requires #20's plugin (which accepts the legacy single-source config too — back-compat is intact).\n4. **Push to gitcloud** as usual; the dev side cherry-picks the field commit onto a follow-up PR per the established field-mode flow.\n\nIf you're not sure which knob to reach for: WiFi telemetry + on-shore agent triage is the safer first step. The producer publishes its lethal grid, so an off-boat agent can subscribe and reason about what the buffer is seeing.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}